  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Owen. Your identity is verified. I found order Q-7601 from Pho Real. The courier's records show it was picked up at 6:22 PM and handed to you in person at 6:41 PM. There are no earlier refunds or credits on this order.\n\nYour order included 2 beef pho at $15.00 each. Since only one was delivered, I can offer you one of two options for the missing pho:\n\n1. **Refund to your original payment method (Visa ending 4242): $12.00.** Your order had a $10.00 WELCOME10 promo, and the pho's share of that discount ($3.00) is not refunded to your card.\n2. **Account credit: $18.00.** This is the pho's full price plus 20%, usable on future Forkful orders.\n\nWhich would you prefer?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hmm, I don't really follow the $12 thing. I didn't know about any WELCOME10 code, I just used a welcome promo when I signed up. Did I get charged $30 for the pho or what? I'd really rather have the money back on my card than store credit."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You were charged $49.74 in total, not $30 for the pho. That total covers the whole order:\n\n- Food: 2 beef pho at $15.00 each, 1 spring rolls at $7.00, 1 banh mi at $13.00 = $50.00\n- Welcome promo discount: -$10.00\n- Delivery fee $2.99, service fee $3.75, and tip $3.00\n\nThe welcome promo reduced the whole order by $10. Each item gets a share of that discount based on its price, so the missing pho's share is $3.00 ($10 \u00d7 $15 \u00f7 $50).\n\nFor the missing pho, that means:\n- **Card refund:** $15.00 minus its $3.00 share of the discount = **$12.00** to your Visa ending 4242.\n- The $3.00 discount share can't go back to your card. Under our policy it's returned as account credit instead, so I can add that $3.00 to your account.\n\nI can't refund the delivery fee, service fee, or tip, since those weren't tied to the missing item.\n\nWould you like me to process the $12.00 refund to your card, plus the $3.00 account credit for the promo share? If you'd rather have the full $12.00 with no credit, I can do that too."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok so basically I get $12 back on my card and $3 in credit? That's a bit of a weird split but fine, I just want the money off my card. Can you process the $12 to the card? And if you can do the full $12 without the credit thing, that would be better, I don't really want credit on the app."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I can process the $12.00 refund to your Visa ending 4242, but I can't drop the $3.00 account credit. The policy says the promo share of an item refund has to come back as account credit, so the card refund and credit go together. I also can't pay the $3.00 to your card.\n\nHere's what I'd do:\n- **$12.00 refunded to your Visa ending 4242** for the missing beef pho\n- **$3.00 added as account credit** for the promo share\n\nShould I go ahead with that? If you'd rather not take the $3.00 credit, the other option is $18.00 in account credit for the whole pho, but that's all credit with nothing on your card."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok fine, go ahead with the $12 to my Visa and the $3 credit. I'd rather have the card money than the full $18 in credit. Thanks for sorting it."
  },
